Subject: [PATCH] fix(display): log the requested brightness, not the level twice

The non-nits request log prints goal twice:

    IOLog("K60 BACKLIGHT: brightness level %u -> level %u dbv 0x%x\n",
          goal, goal, ...)

so the first field cannot tell the raw IODisplayParameters value from the
level it mapped to. The 27 evidence line reads exactly this field to prove
what CoreBrightness sends at both ends of the slider; with goal twice the
line is self-fulfilling and cannot distinguish "asked for 0x0800" from
"asked for level 128".

Keep the requested value in a local and log that. No behaviour change: the
level, the counter, the work-loop request and the published value are the
ones computed before.

Found while writing docs/research/display/DISPLAY-27-INTEGRATION.md (2.1).
Not applied: patches/proposed is a staging area, nothing in the series
reads it.
---
diff --git a/drivers/PongAdreno/K60Backlight.cpp b/drivers/PongAdreno/K60Backlight.cpp
--- a/drivers/PongAdreno/K60Backlight.cpp
+++ b/drivers/PongAdreno/K60Backlight.cpp
@@ -386,4 +386,5 @@
     OSDictionary *dictionary = OSDynamicCast(OSDictionary, properties);
     if (!dictionary) return kIOReturnBadArgument;
     uint32_t goal;
+    uint32_t requested = 0;
     uint32_t milliseconds = 0;
@@ -397,4 +398,5 @@
     } else if (OSNumber *brightness = OSDynamicCast(OSNumber, dictionary->getObject("brightness"))) {
         OSNumber *fadePeriod = OSDynamicCast(OSNumber, dictionary->getObject("FadePeriod"));
-        goal = k60backlight::clampLevel((int64_t)(int32_t)brightness->unsigned32BitValue());
+        requested = brightness->unsigned32BitValue();
+        goal = k60backlight::clampLevel((int64_t)(int32_t)requested);
         if (fadePeriod)
@@ -415,4 +417,4 @@
     } else {
         IOLog("K60 BACKLIGHT: brightness level %u -> level %u dbv 0x%x\n",
-              goal, goal, (unsigned)k60backlight::dbvFromLevel(goal));
+              requested, goal, (unsigned)k60backlight::dbvFromLevel(goal));
     }
